WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
OK, I would say, no matter what.

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.800
So for example, take the Second Amendment,

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:03.800
which we kind of danced around.

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:04.440
It's not been covered.

00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:05.800
It's come up here and there.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:07.520
You know the debate about the Second Amendment.

00:00:07.520 --> 00:00:10.280
The fundamental debate is one side says it's unlimited.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:11.520
And the other side says, no, no, what they meant

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.480
was the malicious.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.120
They didn't mean, and they had muskets.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.400
They didn't mean AR-15s, right?

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:17.440
So we can have that endless debate, which I really

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:18.680
don't care for about that.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:20.879
But to come back to your point about the constitutional

00:00:20.879 --> 00:00:23.520
principles, the 14th Amendment comes along in the 1860s.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:24.320
So it's pretty old.

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:25.440
It's not as old as America.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.240
But it comes along.

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:27.840
And it's been around for 150 years.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.799
So if you want to get away with it, you want to get rid of it.

00:00:29.799 --> 00:00:32.200
But it was around before 150 million Americans.

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.799
And I'm saying it was around before the United States was

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:34.320
even created.

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.480
It's part of ancient English common law.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.240
If you're born in a place, you're

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.560
a citizen of that place, unless you're

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.439
a child of a foreign diplomat or on a Native American

00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:40.400
reservation.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.520
English common law did not exist simultaneously

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:45.040
as millions of people coming across the border in a year.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.200
Just to get to principles, your argument

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.680
is numbers change everything.

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:50.360
Because we've got so many more people who change the constitution.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.480
Not solely, but absolutely.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.279
The demographics of your immigration

00:00:53.279 --> 00:00:54.439
absolutely change it.

00:00:54.439 --> 00:00:55.520
Can I ask you a question?

00:00:55.919 --> 00:00:57.880
If you got rid of the 14th Amendment,

00:00:57.880 --> 00:00:59.320
what would be in its place?

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:01.320
I think a citizenship task would be fantastic.

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:01.840
What age?

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:02.480
What age?

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:04.400
I think we could administer it in high school.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:05.000
To everyone?

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:05.480
Sure.

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.080
Or just the immigrants?

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:07.279
No, everybody.

00:01:07.279 --> 00:01:09.279
And then if you fail it, you denaturalize

00:01:09.279 --> 00:01:10.879
white American native born?

00:01:10.879 --> 00:01:12.000
Maybe you can't get a government job.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:12.959
You can't denaturalize that dude?

00:01:12.959 --> 00:01:14.279
I think there's plenty of benefits

00:01:14.279 --> 00:01:16.480
that the government offers people that you should not

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:17.839
be able to receive.

00:01:17.839 --> 00:01:19.680
I'll tell you this, right?

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:20.800
This might sound bad.

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:22.959
And I think I don't think people care for me anyway.

00:01:22.959 --> 00:01:24.120
So let me say something you might not like.

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:24.760
Nobody would pass it.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.440
If you have a high school immigration citizenship

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:31.879
test for everyone, I'm guessing the immigrant kids are going

00:01:31.879 --> 00:01:33.199
to outperform the white kids.

00:01:33.199 --> 00:01:35.040
And you might actually end up denaturalizing

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.000
some of the white kids.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.839
And then people here will be really upset.

00:01:37.839 --> 00:01:38.879
And well, hold on.

00:01:38.879 --> 00:01:40.480
And I like to be consistent about this.

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:41.199
That's possible.

00:01:41.199 --> 00:01:42.199
But what I think it would do is it

00:01:42.199 --> 00:01:44.440
would give everybody a larger sense of the importance

00:01:44.440 --> 00:01:45.040
of citizenship.

00:01:45.040 --> 00:01:47.320
So you would say no one born in this country is a citizen?

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:47.720
No one?

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:48.519
Automatically, no.

00:01:48.519 --> 00:01:49.320
Automatically, no.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:50.519
I think we could extend that.

00:01:50.519 --> 00:01:52.800
You know, people who have a heritage in the country.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.720
What are they until they pass the test?

00:01:54.959 --> 00:01:55.760
Undocumented?

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.519
I suppose, yeah.

00:01:56.519 --> 00:01:58.320
They are not able to receive government benefits.

00:01:58.320 --> 00:01:59.879
They're not able to receive government benefits.

00:01:59.879 --> 00:02:01.919
They're not able to apply for these jobs that they're

00:02:01.919 --> 00:02:02.440
offered.

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:02.839
But they're parents are citizens.

00:02:02.839 --> 00:02:04.000
OK, well, hold on.

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:06.320
We're talking here about the way that we would implement it.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.320
Yeah, it's pretty important.

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:08.479
If you're trying to get rid of the 14th Amendment,

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:09.839
I'm going to ask about the practicalities of it.

00:02:09.839 --> 00:02:11.399
And we're not going to do it right now.

00:02:11.399 --> 00:02:12.880
And I'm not going to be able to explain it to you in 10

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:13.080
minutes.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:14.800
But what I can explain to you is that right now in this country,

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:16.839
we have a crisis of people not understanding.

00:02:16.839 --> 00:02:17.639
Hold on.

00:02:17.639 --> 00:02:20.160
We're not understanding what citizenship is.

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.919
The way that you've referred to citizenship

00:02:21.919 --> 00:02:23.839
makes everybody who hasn't come to the United States

00:02:23.839 --> 00:02:26.160
an undocumented American citizen until the time

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:26.880
they come over here.

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:28.000
That's how a lot of countries are, right?

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:29.720
You know that birthright citizenship

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:32.039
is operated by multiple democracies around the world.

00:02:32.039 --> 00:02:33.360
I know Trump lies and says, we're

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.479
the only country that does it.

00:02:34.479 --> 00:02:34.919
He lies.

00:02:34.919 --> 00:02:35.679
That's not true.

00:02:35.679 --> 00:02:36.399
Multiple countries have birthright citizenship.

00:02:36.399 --> 00:02:37.399
Do you think it ought to be that way?

00:02:37.399 --> 00:02:38.559
Do you think everybody in the world

00:02:38.559 --> 00:02:39.720
is an undocumented American?

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:41.520
So hold on.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:42.880
Or undocumented Canadian.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.399
Or undocumented Brit, right?

00:02:44.399 --> 00:02:45.199
Or undocumented Jew?

00:02:45.199 --> 00:02:45.679
Sure.

00:02:45.679 --> 00:02:47.360
Well, I'm an American, so I say America.

00:02:47.360 --> 00:02:47.839
But yeah, it could be anything.

00:02:47.839 --> 00:02:49.639
But I'm saying, right, the principle is you immigrate.

00:02:49.639 --> 00:02:50.080
We have free movement.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:50.800
Do you believe that?

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.240
I support free movement of people around the world.

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:53.559
But do you believe they're all undocumented?

00:02:53.559 --> 00:02:54.360
Are you Kim Jong-un?

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:55.720
You think people should only stay in one country

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.559
and never leave and be blocked from leaving their country?

00:02:57.559 --> 00:02:58.839
I think there's a very illiberal,

00:02:58.839 --> 00:02:59.800
unconservative position.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:04.440
I think there's a big room to move between being Kim Jong-un

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.479
and saying that it means.

00:03:05.479 --> 00:03:05.559
Not really.

00:03:05.559 --> 00:03:07.199
In practical terms, if you accept.

00:03:07.199 --> 00:03:08.000
I gave one side.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:08.839
I want to give the other.

00:03:08.839 --> 00:03:11.360
There's a big room to move between being Kim Jong-un

00:03:11.360 --> 00:03:14.839
and saying that everybody in the world is an American.

00:03:14.839 --> 00:03:16.360
They're just not on our soil yet.

00:03:16.360 --> 00:03:17.360
I think being an American citizen.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:18.240
I mean, that's a ridiculous statement, right?

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.119
Because everyone in the world is not

00:03:19.119 --> 00:03:19.880
heading for the United States of America.

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:20.199
Yes.

00:03:20.199 --> 00:03:22.240
In fact, right now, the numbers of people coming in

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:22.600
are dropping a lot.

00:03:22.600 --> 00:03:24.440
But the idea that you are supporting

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:26.800
is that the moment you come to this soil

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:28.839
and that you're born here, you become an American.

00:03:28.839 --> 00:03:30.320
So I'm not saying at the moment you come to this soil,

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:30.919
you become an American.

00:03:30.919 --> 00:03:31.639
I didn't.

00:03:31.639 --> 00:03:32.520
I had to do the test.

00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:32.960
OK.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:34.559
I had to do the naturalization process, which

00:03:34.559 --> 00:03:35.800
is guaranteed by the 14th Amendment.

00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:38.479
But the 14th Amendment also says, if you're born here,

00:03:38.479 --> 00:03:39.800
then you automatically get it.

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.279
And I'm not saying it's a hill I'm going to die on.

00:03:42.279 --> 00:03:46.559
The problem we have is we don't appreciate citizenship.

00:03:46.559 --> 00:03:48.279
The problem is that when you talk about immigration

00:03:48.279 --> 00:03:49.839
like we did before, when we talked

00:03:49.839 --> 00:03:51.360
about everything before, what were we talking about?

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:52.279
We were talking about products.

00:03:52.279 --> 00:03:54.360
We weren't talking about practices or perceptions,

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:56.320
which is really what immigration is about.

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:57.119
Can I agree with you?

00:03:57.119 --> 00:03:58.919
We don't, in this country, value citizenship enough.

00:03:58.919 --> 00:03:59.279
I agree.

00:03:59.279 --> 00:04:00.360
I think we should encourage people

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:02.479
to have more civics lessons in schools,

00:04:02.479 --> 00:04:04.800
understand American history and Constitution much more.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:05.919
Here's what the irony is.

00:04:05.919 --> 00:04:07.300
I'm sitting in a room today where

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.800
I've met a bunch of people claiming

00:04:08.800 --> 00:04:11.399
to be Native Americans who hate everything America

00:04:11.399 --> 00:04:12.440
stood for for centuries.

00:04:12.440 --> 00:04:14.240
I think they stand much closer to the America

00:04:14.240 --> 00:04:15.080
that we originally had.

00:04:15.080 --> 00:04:15.720
And I think that's the big disagreement.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:16.480
I don't think any of you live there

00:04:16.480 --> 00:04:17.640
or had any clue what that was like.

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:19.200
But you've agreed to dismantling it.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.200
I don't know things about that America.

00:04:20.200 --> 00:04:21.839
But you've agreed to dismantling that America

00:04:21.839 --> 00:04:22.679
as long as it's legal.

00:04:22.679 --> 00:04:23.040
You have.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:24.679
You're the person who came here and made your argument.

00:04:24.679 --> 00:04:25.799
I'm a Constitutional originalist.

00:04:25.799 --> 00:04:26.559
Take it away, take it away, an amendment

00:04:26.559 --> 00:04:27.119
of the Constitution.

00:04:27.119 --> 00:04:27.359
I did.

00:04:27.359 --> 00:04:28.239
I said, keep the Second Amendment.

00:04:28.239 --> 00:04:29.000
I'm an originalist.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.519
I think we should interpret it the way it was probably

00:04:30.519 --> 00:04:32.040
originally interpreted.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:34.000
All right, guys, that's time.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:35.239
Nice to speak with you, Kite.

00:04:35.239 --> 00:04:36.079
Thank you very much.

00:04:36.079 --> 00:04:38.880
Appreciate it.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.200
I thought it would be an interesting exercise in trying

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:44.519
to understand what genuine, far-right, conservative folks

00:04:44.519 --> 00:04:45.200
think.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:46.679
And it was kind of disturbing to see

00:04:46.679 --> 00:04:47.959
that they think what I thought they'd think.

00:04:47.959 --> 00:04:49.079
And they were happy to say it out loud.

00:04:49.119 --> 00:04:51.679
I am disappointed that I had to sit across from people

00:04:51.679 --> 00:04:54.600
who believe in white genocide, who believe I'm not a citizen.

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.920
Multiple people here said I should be deported.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:58.640
One of them was even the child of immigrants,

00:04:58.640 --> 00:04:59.839
which I found bizarre.

00:04:59.839 --> 00:05:02.040
Obviously, we were way outclassed.

00:05:02.040 --> 00:05:05.160
Like, we're not professional debaters.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.359
I don't think anyone in this room was.

00:05:06.359 --> 00:05:07.920
Maybe one or two people.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:10.760
And clearly, Manny, he does this for a living, right?

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:11.799
He's a journalist.

00:05:11.799 --> 00:05:13.480
So he's really good at what he does.

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:16.119
Mehdi Hassan was pretty good at taking cheap shots,

00:05:16.119 --> 00:05:19.760
trying to derail people from their arguments,

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:21.839
trying to pit me against some of the people

00:05:21.839 --> 00:05:23.519
that wouldn't like people of my color

00:05:23.519 --> 00:05:25.959
to be in the United States, which is irrelevant.

00:05:25.959 --> 00:05:27.279
I think one person said, if you walked off,

00:05:27.279 --> 00:05:30.959
you'll be the first to go, which is ominous and racist.

00:05:30.959 --> 00:05:34.079
I think that was disheartening and particularly discouraging,

00:05:34.079 --> 00:05:36.399
because it just felt like it was fitting into a stereotype

00:05:36.399 --> 00:05:37.399
that we're trying to fight against,

00:05:37.399 --> 00:05:38.760
which is like, we actually have arguments.

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:40.079
We can provide good reason.

00:05:40.079 --> 00:05:42.200
And that rhetoric just pushes that far away.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.320
I am, I guess, a far-right Republican.

00:05:44.399 --> 00:05:45.880
But as I learned today, not as far-right

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:46.799
as I thought I was.

00:05:46.799 --> 00:05:48.679
You know, someone gets up and they're just like,

00:05:48.679 --> 00:05:50.640
yeah, I mean, I guess I just want to have, like,

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:53.279
autocracy forever and Christian nationalism,

00:05:53.279 --> 00:05:55.399
or just being like, yeah, I'm racist.

00:05:55.399 --> 00:05:57.839
And to me, that's very foreign of a concept.

00:05:57.839 --> 00:05:59.679
While I didn't, you know, disagree with most of the people

00:05:59.679 --> 00:06:01.559
in the circle, it did bother me at times, you know,

00:06:01.559 --> 00:06:03.600
to see them say mean things.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:05.239
There's not really a reason to do that.

00:06:05.239 --> 00:06:06.880
But it also upset me when Mehdi said, you know,

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:08.839
I'm not willing to debate with those people.

00:06:08.839 --> 00:06:11.399
Free speech doesn't mean you need to give credibility

00:06:11.399 --> 00:06:14.720
or oxygen or a platform to people who don't agree

00:06:14.720 --> 00:06:15.799
in human equality.

00:06:15.799 --> 00:06:18.440
I hear Mehdi's point about not giving them a platform.

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:21.079
But the thing is, if you stop giving them a platform,

00:06:21.079 --> 00:06:23.119
they don't just go away and change their mind.

00:06:23.119 --> 00:06:25.160
And then you tell the rest of society,

00:06:25.160 --> 00:06:26.519
no one exists who thinks like that.

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:27.359
And that's not true.

00:06:27.359 --> 00:06:29.640
I do like to debate people, even people I disagree with.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:31.640
I try and avoid bad faith folks.

00:06:31.640 --> 00:06:33.880
I think some of the folks today were bad faith.

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:36.160
You know, I'm anti-conservative, right?

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.679
I don't support conservative views on taxation.

00:06:38.679 --> 00:06:41.000
I don't support conservative views on immigration.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.279
But the people here today were way beyond conservatives.

00:06:43.279 --> 00:06:45.000
This is open authoritarianism.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:47.160
And this is what is being normalized and mainstreamed

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:50.079
in our country by people in power, by the media,

00:06:50.079 --> 00:06:51.880
by people who don't know any better.

